      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "As the survival of renal transplant patients has increased, so has their risk of significant morbidity. Immunosuppressive drugs can exacerbate preexisting conditions and promote development of new disease. Effective long-term care of transplant recipients requires an understanding of how these drugs affect clinical evaluations and treatments."},
